sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Public client (PublicConnection)
    participant R as public_rpc (vcp-lifecycle)
    participant H as Retained lifecycle host
    participant E as vcp-engine public.rs
    participant S as Canonical store
    C->>R: steering command (durable command ID)
    R->>H: seal admission (admission proof)
    H->>H: pause tasks (pause proof)
    H->>H: drain owner work (shared concurrent drain)
    R->>E: revalidate controller lease
    alt controller lost or worker fenced
        E-->>S: record interrupted authority intent (no receipt)
    else controller still valid
        E->>S: commit original durable command + receipt
    end
    Note over C,R: Dropping the request waiter does not abandon completion
    C--xR: disconnect
    R->>H: pause, drain, release lease
    Note over H,S: Observers and canonical writer stay alive
